{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1981 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "59495d4577b39f3342f66f4654850246d81da4cdcde1feb1b9cffd883dd0b581" :edb/db-before-t 1980 :edb/db-after-t 1981 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535293 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:26:30.442Z" 13194139535293 true] [17592186078517 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342214 13194139535293 true] [17592186078518 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342218 13194139535293 true] [17592186078518 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342221 13194139535293 true] [17592186293780 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061763/assets/d36f2859865da58d226a738d8338f726df950db75b7421b604bb692c9049d54a.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 true] [17592186293780 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/d36f2859865da58d226a738d8338f726df950db75b7421b604bb692c9049d54a.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 false] [17592186293783 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061763/assets/8eb7c4fe147028c6dc31aad2427a33bb713553e610101b1fd263bda30f5c49d0.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 true] [17592186293783 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/8eb7c4fe147028c6dc31aad2427a33bb713553e610101b1fd263bda30f5c49d0.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 false] [17592186342214 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342215 13194139535293 true] [17592186342214 1089 "q-316132" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342214 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535293 true] [17592186342214 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061763/assets/b871a949beaac0319d77364c43aa261bda8c28642f8bfc80a80f974fd7323cf3.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 true] [17592186342214 1113 #uuid "701dff71-e2c9-5a39-9c92-e7e127a3d233" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342214 1145 "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-2,-1],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-1,1),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,-1].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a square, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-2+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342216 13194139535293 true] [17592186342215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342217 13194139535293 true] [17592186342215 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535293 true] [17592186342215 1041 "field-1" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342215 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342217 13194139535293 true] [17592186342215 1110 #uuid "0867d975-b31a-5413-b1c9-724054d513ae" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342216 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535293 true] [17592186342216 1111 #uuid "e11e6707-d2e2-5fee-afc6-46454c46a61f" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342217 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535293 true] [17592186342217 1111 #uuid "a3973676-5332-57e8-a724-95d70a4ba495" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342218 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342219 13194139535293 true] [17592186342218 1089 "q-338511" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342218 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535293 true] [17592186342218 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061763/assets/def5dbb4e5a338159e09c098e47e0b78cbe59d31bcd67478f4dbb7b1c85488f9.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 true] [17592186342218 1113 #uuid "9e602f85-6313-5b1e-91a0-e275215905a2" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342218 1145 "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the arc of the quarter circle for $x\\in [-2,1)$ and the line segment for $x\\in [1,5].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,1).$ The corresponding region is a quarter circle of radius $3,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi \\cdot (3)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi +16}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342220 13194139535293 true] [17592186342219 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535293 true] [17592186342219 1041 "field-1" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342219 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342220 13194139535293 true] [17592186342219 1110 #uuid "f4b917c2-594f-5e61-a022-6fcda75fcdb8" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342220 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi}{4}+4" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535293 true] [17592186342220 1111 #uuid "7b03183e-f29b-5823-8cd8-e02d3a36e2b4" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342221 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342222 13194139535293 true] [17592186342221 1089 "q-339679" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342221 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535293 true] [17592186342221 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061763/assets/38270fdcb312cdce6a76e1d88bfa0117b4a69b5024b2acfd0456646471ead71f.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535293 true] [17592186342221 1113 #uuid "080d27d4-373a-55c7-9b81-6a1bc5f1e92a" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342221 1145 "The graph consists of $4$ parts: the arc of the quarter-circle for \n$x\\in [-6,-4),$ the line segment for $x\\in (-4,-1],$ the line segment for \n$x\\in (-1,1],$ and the arc of the quarter-circle for $x\\in [1,5].$ \nTherefore, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-6}^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{4}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the\n$x$-axis, where $x\\in [-6,-4).$ The corresponding region is a rectangle minus a quarter-circle of radius $2,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =(2)(2)-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=\\pi -4.\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-4,-1].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-1,1].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3+1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region is a combination of a semi-circle of radius $2$ and a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =bh+\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =1(4)+\\frac{1}{2}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =4+2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =\\pi -4+3+4+4+2\\pi  \\\\  & =7+3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342223 13194139535293 true] [17592186342222 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535293 true] [17592186342222 1041 "field-1" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342222 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342223 13194139535293 true] [17592186342222 1110 #uuid "d1f94c02-3c0b-5f46-a640-b274177f4906" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342223 1034 "3\\pi+7" 13194139535293 true] [17592186342223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535293 true] [17592186342223 1111 #uuid "5e9fbfef-1271-5f1b-9d8a-ff0eb8a31264" 13194139535293 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-316132" 17592186342214 "q-316132/field-1" 17592186342215 "q-316132/field-1/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" 17592186342216 "q-316132/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" 17592186342217 "q-338511" 17592186342218 "q-338511/field-1" 17592186342219 "q-338511/field-1/3a3822ca8679744117bf695217b55cf9606da24fd9bfad29a203f66a070cc4bf" 17592186342220 "q-339679" 17592186342221 "q-339679/field-1" 17592186342222 "q-339679/field-1/5fe9489e4f686c8a33882f119ff8cc7e1d08759a0c131de787be5b622394af73" 17592186342223}}
